From 61df41a5cf94c81aac0d64b8a05d0f089e3d8b51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chen Jun <newdays-cj@live.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:48:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH v2 1/8] arm64: mm: populate vmemmap PTE tables during fallback

Only treat a PMD block as an already populated vmemmap range. An existing PTE table may still contain empty entries after an early allocation failure and must be completed by base-page population.

Without this distinction, falling back from boot-time HugeTLB vmemmap preparation can leave an empty PTE and fault during struct page initialization.

Signed-off-by: Chen Jun <newdays-cj@live.com>
Co-authored-by: sisyphus-dev-ai <sisyphus-dev-ai@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/mm/mmu.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/mm/mmu.c b/arch/arm64/mm/mmu.c
index 6ffd7305ee80..edc877ba1b41 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/mm/mmu.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/mm/mmu.c
@@ -1636,6 +1636,8 @@ void __meminit vmemmap_set_pmd(pmd_t *pmdp, void *p, int node,
 int __meminit vmemmap_check_pmd(pmd_t *pmdp, int node,
 				unsigned long addr, unsigned long next)
 {
+	if (!pmd_sect(pmdp_get(pmdp)))
+		return 0;
 	vmemmap_verify((pte_t *)pmdp, node, addr, next);
 	return 1;
 }
